 "citation": "Kerala Antimicrobial Resistance Surveillance Network (KARS-Net). Annual Report 2026 (Data from 1 January to 31 December 2025). Thiruvananthapuram: Department of Microbiology, Government Medical College, Thiruvananthapuram (state nodal centre), Kerala Antimicrobial Resistance Strategic Action Plan (KARSAP), Department of Health Services, Kerala; 2026.",
 "reporting": "Percent resistant by pathogen and specimen (blood, pus aspirate, other sterile body fluids, urine; stool for Salmonella and Shigella), all location types pooled, with number tested and number resistant; blood isolates also charted by location type (OPD, IPD, ICU) with printed data labels; MRSA and VRE yearly trend charts.",
 "method": "WHONET collation and analysis; CLSI interpretive criteria; disc diffusion, broth microdilution and automated AST at the sites; colistin by broth microdilution or agar dilution per the NARS-Net SOP; first isolate per patient, specimen type and pathogen (73,437 isolates reported, 65,849 unique-patient isolates). Percentages not computed when fewer than 30 isolates were tested.",
 "breakpoints": "CLSI, edition not stated",
 "measure": "R",
 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Tables 4 to 11 parsed from the PDF text layer (pdfplumber words assigned to columns by x position) and every value compared by eye with the pages rendered at scale 2.2; each printed percentage was also recomputed from its printed counts (four disagreements are recorded as conflicts). Figures 7 to 12 (blood by location): data labels taken from the text layer in top-to-bottom order and checked on the rendered chart against bar position and legend colour (OPD grey, IPD orange, ICU blue); the text statement for Pseudomonas ceftazidime (ICU 39%, IPD 24%, OPD 25%) confirms the colour order. MRSA and VRE trend labels read from the rendered charts (one bar per year in legend order). Count Tables 2 and 3 checked against the images and their printed totals. Page numbers are 1-based PDF pages."
 },
 "notes": "Kerala state antibiogram (KARS-Net Annual Report 2026, released September 2026), data from 1 January to 31 December 2025: 55 of 59 network laboratories in 14 districts (government and private medical colleges, government hospitals and laboratories, private hospitals). All figures are percent resistant (intermediate counted as not resistant). Specimen PA (pus aspirate) is shown under deep infections (aspirates) and OSBF (other sterile body fluids) as sterile. The specimen tables pool all location types (set all); blood rows by location (OPD, IPD, ICU) come from the bar charts. The Salmonella table covers blood and stool isolates together (recorded as all specimens). The all-specimen S. aureus (cefoxitin) and Enterococcus (vancomycin) rows carry the MRSA and VRE yearly trends. Drugs printed \"-\" (fewer than 30 tested) are left out.",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: 122 of 487 cells (seeded 25% sample over all 16 tables and charts), all 46 row n values and all 51 counts read from the page images (scale 2.5 to 5, dense charts cropped into halves) before comparing with the extraction: 0 transcription errors; organism, specimen and OPD/IPD/ICU setting correct on every sampled row.",
  "Whole-file cross-checks: an independent word-position parse of Tables 4 to 11 matched all 284 printed percentages and every number tested; the vector bars of Figures 7 to 12 confirmed that each of the 201 chart labels belongs to the recorded drug and location (bar position and legend colour, OPD grey, IPD orange, ICU blue; zero labels by position) and equals its bar length, except the one below; MRSA and VRE trend labels agree with their bar heights.",
  "Conflicts confirmed accurate as recorded (each row re-read on a scale-4 crop): Klebsiella pus doxycycline 45% (227 of 580 = 39%), Pseudomonas blood netilmicin 21% (19 of 126 = 15%), S. Typhi azithromycin 3% (1 of 73 = 1.4%), S. Paratyphi cotrimoxazole 0% (1 of 44 = 2.3%). Added one the extraction missed: Figure 12 Acinetobacter blood OPD minocycline is labelled 17% but its bar is drawn at 11% (label kept, conflict entry added).",
  "Printed percentages that differ from their own counts by rounding only (under 1 point, left without a conflict): for example Shigella cotrimoxazole 47% (33 of 71 = 46.5%), E. coli blood ertapenem 13% (119 of 953 = 12.5%), Enterococcus urine vancomycin 2% (46 of 3125 = 1.5%).",
  "Lead 2026-09-26: \"PA (pus aspirate)\" (NCDC SOP category, aspirated pus, swabs excluded) filed under specimen \"deep\" (deep infections, aspirates), as for NARS-Net, TARS-Net and AARSNET; 6 rows and 6 counts moved from \"pus\"."
 ],
